# Carryon's default exclude patterns, installed as /usr/share/carryon/excludes.default.
#
# Restic pattern rules: "*" stays inside one folder, "**" spans any number of folders, a leading
# "/" anchors the pattern at the root, and a matching folder is left out with everything in it.
# One pattern per line; comments go on their own line.
#
# Only things every machine has go here. What belongs to one app (Steam games, toolchains, browser
# caches) is in that app's catalog file, which also says how it comes back after a restore.
# To keep one of these in the backup, switch it off in the config (backup.skip_default_excludes).

# Caches: apps refill them as needed. The XDG standard says nothing in them may be needed later.
/home/*/.cache
/root/.cache

# Flatpak apps' caches: the same thing, inside each app's own folder.
/home/*/.var/app/*/cache

# The trash: deleted on purpose, and often large.
/home/*/.local/share/Trash
/root/.local/share/Trash

# KDE's file search index (Baloo): rebuilt from your files after a restore.
/home/*/.local/share/baloo
